  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 102.11 Amended water",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 102.11 “Amended water” means water to which a chemical wetting agent, such as a surfactant, has been added to improve penetration of the water into asbestos or other materials to limit the potential for airborne particulates.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 102.05) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
